# madcide "vivid" scheme: the original colourful look (the pre-JOE-parity
# default) — every class gets a colour, including the AST-backed function
# class JOE doesn't have. Swap with ^K T.
keyword yellow
type green
string red
number magenta
comment cyan
function bold blue

# @gui workbench colours for the vivid scheme (a warmer accent).
@gui bg #201a24
@gui fg #ece4f0
@gui accent #f0a35e

# @presence (client-server V3c): the caret colours dealt round-robin to
# clients at connect (a slot per line; the window renders another client's
# caret in its slot colour, the TUI ignores these). Eight distinguishable
# entries over the sixteen-colour palette (bold = bright).
@presence 0 cyan
@presence 1 magenta
@presence 2 yellow
@presence 3 green
@presence 4 red
@presence 5 blue
@presence 6 bold cyan
@presence 7 bold magenta
